 "source": "CPF Board, EdgeProp, MoneySmart",
 "caption": "Bought a $1.5 million condo? In about year 19, your CPF could stop paying the loan. 🏦\n\nFor private property, CPF use is capped at the price or valuation, whichever is lower, including your downpayment. Pay $300,000 down from CPF and about $5,300 a month from CPF, and you hit that cap around year 19. You can go up to 120%, $1.8M, only if you've set aside your Basic Retirement Sum. After that, every instalment is cash.\n\nUseful info? Follow for more 👇\n\nIllustration: $1.125M loan, 3%, 25 years, all instalments from CPF. CPF Board rules.",
